{{also|Rowan}}
==English==
[[File:Rowan tree 20081002b.jpg|right|thumb|A European rowan]]

===Etymology===
From Northern English or Scottish, of {{etyl|non|en}} origin: compare {{term|reynir|lang=non}}; compare Norwegian {{term|rogn|lang=no}}, Danish {{term|røn|lang=da}}. Ultimately related to the root of {{term|red|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/rəʊən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/roʊən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# ''[[Sorbus aucuparia]]'', the [[European rowan]].
# Any of various small [[deciduous]] [[tree]]s or [[shrub]]s of genus ''[[Sorbus]]'', belonging to the rose family, with [[pinnate]] leaves, [[corymb]]s of white flowers, and usually with orange-red berries.

